{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And strong drink.</b> That made from a species of wheat, or honey, or dates. For wine corrupts the intellect of its drinkers, and matters become confused for them. Therefore, 'and to distinguish' — for you are a high priest, and you shall distinguish between the sacred precinct and the profane — this is from the root of חלול. It is also possible: between a sacred day and the profane."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:16.977427497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}